WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:04.133
We are hanging out
with Chelsea Handler now!

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.133
-I'm here.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.467
-We were talking
earlier about --

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.033
about how great you were
on "The Daily Show."

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.434
And I just like that you're able
to just speak your mind

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.834
and say whatever you want
about whatever you want to say.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:19.067
And it's very funny,
but it's very honest.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.300
It's very you.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.167
And I thought maybe
it'd be a fun game

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:25.033
if you just helped everyone with
their life decisions out there.

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.300
And we got a bunch of questions.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.934
It is time for "Life Coach
with Chelsea Handler."

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.267
Here we go.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.334
-♪ Life Coach ♪

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:35.367
♪ With Chelsea Handler ♪

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.567
-I love it.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.934
-Are you ready to give out
some tough advice?

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.367
-Yeah, no problem.
I love this.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.400
-You'll be great at this.
Right.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.067
No order, but I'll just
start with this one.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.501
-"I went to a dry wedding,
but the problem --"

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.467
-Ugh.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.801
So annoying.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:53.133
That's so annoying
to have a dry wedding.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:55.434
-"The problem is --"
That wasn't the problem.

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:58.100
-Oh, oh, okay.
-"The problem is I'm not dry

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.133
and brought some booze."
-Right.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.767
-"Now the bride and groom
won't talk to me.

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.067
Should I apologize?"

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.167
-I would just say, yeah,
you can apologize,

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.934
but just also stop
being friends with them.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.334
You know what I mean?

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.868
What's the point?
What's the point?

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.234
Like, you like drinking.
They're dry.

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.334
Like, just end it
and just go out with people

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.767
that you enjoy
having a good time with.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.801
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.367
-Just end the --
-I mean, it's not complicated.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:19.501
No.
-Not complicated.

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:20.501
"We're not friends anymore."

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.000
-But, no,
you can say you're sorry,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.701
but they shouldn't be having a
dry wedding in the first place.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:24.868
That's not thinking of others.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.534
That's only thinking of,
you know.

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:27.534
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:28.767
-Selfish.
-Yeah, you're coming

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.133
to a wedding,
you're bringing a gift.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:32.100
You could at least throw me
a Long Island iced tea

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.934
or something, you know?

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:37.000
-Yeah, it doesn't have to
be top-shelf or anything.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.834
-Well...
-Alright. This one says...

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.968
-Well, that's annoying, too,

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:49.400
because if she's
your best friend,

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.400
she should know that's
how you like to exit a party.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.601
You know, I don't have anything
wrong with an Irish exit.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:54.701
When people say goodbye --

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.601
or they leave
without saying goodbye,

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:57.601
I don't mind that.

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:58.968
I've done it plenty of times.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.000
I've done it in my own house
at a dinner party.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.200
I've just -- I have.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.100
I mean, I just am done
with the company

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.000
and I wrap things up
and I just go to bed, you know.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.167
-And they're still eating.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.968
-They can still hang out.
Have fun.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:13.667
I love hearing laughter
and joyousness in my own house,

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:15.000
especially when I'm in my room.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.000
I loved that feeling,
that familial, you know?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.300
-It lulls you to sleep.
-Yeah, yeah, so...

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.434
But also, you know,
your friend should understand

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:24.567
if you make an Irish exit,

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:25.567
that's not the worst thing
in the world.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:26.734
Who cares about that?
-Yeah.

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:29.267
So don't be friends with them.
-Well, I mean...

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:30.734
-I'm adding the worst advice.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.267
-I don't know
how many friendships

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:35.200
I want to break up tonight,
so let's go one by one by one.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.100
-Yeah, okay, perfect. Yeah.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.601
Alright, this one is...

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:54.501
-You definitely do not have to
go to a dog's birthday party.

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:56.901
That's a very annoying friend
also, quite frankly.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.200
You know what I mean?

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.934
It's one thing to have
a birthday party for a dog.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.400
It's another thing
to register for that dog.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.667
Like, that's a little bit much.
-It's a bit much.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.701
-Everybody needs to --
You need to look within

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.167
and figure out why everyone
is friends with each other,

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.567
because it doesn't add up.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.834
-Yeah. Have you ever gone
to a dog's birthday party?

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.000
-No, and I never would.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.801
I mean, I'd sooner
go to a cat --

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:19.200
No, I wouldn't go to a cat's
birthday party, either.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.667
But I wouldn't go
to a dog's birthday party.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.334
-You love dogs.
-I do love dogs,

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:26.367
but I don't know when
their birthdays are, you know?

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.634
And it's not important.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.300
Like, I'm not celebrating
a dog's birthday.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.634
-Okay. Yeah. Okay.
Absolutely not.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.234
This one's not about birthdays.

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.100
It seems like the last two
or three are about birthdays.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.033
-I'm like a birthday wrecker.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.100
-Alright, Chelsea.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.067
-Yes!

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.067
Yes, you should
call him out on it.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:49.200
-Yeah.
-Oh. Oh, I see. Camera off.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.367
Not just, like, from up.
Okay.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.133
I was thinking about,
you know --

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.367
You know what I was
thinking about.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.734
Camera off.
-People don't do that.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.300
-No, sometimes people
are insecure on-camera, I think.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.701
Right?

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:02.968
I'm not, so I don't know
what other people are thinking,

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.000
but people -- Right?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.734
Some people don't want
to be on-camera.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.033
Right? Yeah.
Respect that.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:08.667
-I don't know.
They're kind of divided, I feel.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:09.734
-Are you?

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.167
-Well, I think
if you're on a Zoom call,

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.834
I think go back
to the phone call.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.033
I think we're good
with the Zooms.

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:15.767
-I would love to go back
to phone calls,

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.367
and I would also like
to make an announcement

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:18.834
that I don't like FaceTime

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:21.000
and I don't want people
to continue to FaceTime me.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.334
That is an assault.

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:23.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.701
-What are you talking about?

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.834
-People random-- Like, you
have to make an appointment

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.334
to talk to me
on the phone face-to-face.

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:31.067
I'm not just going to pick up
and be like, "Whoo!"

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:34.100
No, I hate that.
I hate it.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.734
-Yeah, you have to
make an appointment.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.534
-Yeah.
-I agree. It's a bit much.

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:39.367
Yeah, too much.
How about this?

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.601
-You're the music guy,
aren't you?

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.300
I mean, you help him
make a decision, Jimmy.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.934
This one is on you.
-These are movies.

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:54.934
-Oh.

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:59.033
"PAW Patrol."
-"PAW Patrol"?

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:00.634
It's a cartoon.

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:03.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.667
Did you mean Snow Patrol?

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:08.868
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:11.267
-I think you meant Snow Patrol.
-Oh, my God.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.934
-"PAW Patrol"
is a cartoon for kids.

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.300
-I know.
I defer to you guys on music.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.334
You know this.

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:19.567
-"PAW Patrol" or "Saw"?
I don't know.

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:20.901
-I don't know.
They both sound like --

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.200
One sounds like it's about
a dog's birthday party,

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.801
and the other one --

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:26.200
-Sounds like a FaceTime.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:29.868
It's everything we talked about.

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:32.934
Yeah, stay home. Yeah.

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:35.234
Don't be friends
with your husband.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.434
Alright.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:37.934
-"The holidays are coming up,

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:38.834
and I'm dreading
spending time --"

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.167
-Already?

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:41.267
-It is.
-It's October.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:42.267
What do you mean?

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:43.434
-Have you been to a CVS?

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:46.033
-No, I haven't.
-It's merry Christmas.

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.200
-Oh, really?
-Happy Hanukkah.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.167
-Already?
-It's happening, absolutely.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.601
-Isn't there a big holiday
that has to come before that?

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:54.133
Like, Thanksgiving or Oct--
-And Halloween.

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:55.634
-Yeah, Halloween,

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:58.067
before we head right into
Christmas and Hanukkah.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:05:59.501
-No.
-Oh, that means I'm going to

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:01.767
see my family again soon.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.100
-That's what this is.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:16.968
-A good way to handle
that situation

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:20.801
is to tell your husband's
parents, who sound Republican,

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.434
that you are thinking about --

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.868
that you are thinking
about transitioning.

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:27.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.567 --> 00:06:33.934
Sit down!

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:35.567
Look at him.

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.167
-That is all the time we have

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:39.634
with "Life Coach
with Chelsea Handler."

